"""What Helvy (the HELVY Connect assistant, formerly "HELV Assistant") knows about HelloVoice and the portal, beyond the live
data its tools read. Written from the portal itself and HelloVoice's answers
(2026-10-08). Facts here are stable policy and how-to; anything numeric about
creators, prices, selections or campaigns always comes from the tools.

Admins can add notes in Client portal → Settings (kb_text); they are appended.
"""

KNOWLEDGE = """
ABOUT HELLOVOICE
- HelloVoice is BlueHolding's film and media production house in Al-Olaya, Riyadh, working mainly with healthcare and pharma brands, plus FMCG, retail and tech.
- Services: (1) video production (brand, launch, patient-awareness and documentary films); (2) influencer campaigns end to end: casting, brief and script, production, compliance, tracking and reporting; (3) technology activations (mixed reality, VR, hologram, interactive screens, projection).
- Influencer markets: Saudi Arabia, UAE and Egypt.
- Contact: info@hellovoice.co.uk, +966 11 463 4518. Replies within one working day. NDA on request.

HOW A CAMPAIGN RUNS
- Steps: shortlist creators → request a quote → the account manager confirms creators, deliverables, dates and price → contract or PO → brief and script → production → compliance check → posting → tracking and report.
- Timeline: usually 2–3 weeks from an approved quote until the content is live.
- Revisions, content usage rights (including paid/ads use), payment terms and cancellation are agreed per campaign in the quote and contract. The account manager confirms them; never promise specific terms.

CREATORS AND VETTING
- Every creator in the catalogue is reviewed by the HelloVoice team for content quality and brand safety, and their follower numbers are checked against the live platform.
- Many creators have a full analysis (audience countries, gender and ages, engagement, average views, fake followers); others show public numbers only. Clients can press "Request full analysis" on a creator's page and the team adds it.
- Advertising licences are shown as "Verified ✓" stamps when checked: the Saudi Mawthooq licence and the UAE licence. The catalogue can be filtered by licence.
- Healthcare professionals (HCP) are a separate group of creators (doctors, pharmacists and similar), with their own tiers.

PRICES
- Helvy never discusses prices, fees, rates, costs or budgets for creators or HelloVoice, not even ranges. Every pricing question gets the same answer: the account manager prepares a quote (Request a quote on the selection, or ask Helvy to request one).
- The ROI Calculator shows what a selection (or a mix of creator sizes) can deliver as ranges of views, reach, interactions and clicks, labelled as an estimate. It never shows creator or HelloVoice prices, and it gives no cost per result and no verdict against the market.

USING THE PORTAL
- Catalogue: browse vetted creators, filter by platform, size, city or country, topic and licence, and open any creator's analysis in a side panel.
- Shortlisting: tick creators and save them as a selection. A selection has its own link and is opened with its access code; colleagues on the same account share selections and campaigns.
- "Build a shortlist with AI": six quick questions (goal, platforms, the countries of the audience, product space, budget, number of creators) produce a scored shortlist saved as a selection. The Campaign Power meter (out of 1000) shows how complete the brief is. Several answers can be picked for the goal, the platforms, the countries (for example Saudi Arabia and UAE together), the product space and, when asked, the gender (Women and Men together means everyone) and the age groups (for example 18–24 and 25–34). Budget, the number of creators and the start timing take one answer each. The brief is attached to the selection it builds, so every creator in it shows the same score the shortlist gave, and the ROI Calculator opens pre-filled from it (goal, platforms, country and, if given, budget).
- Match score: each creator is scored out of 100 against the brief's goal(s) by comparing them with creators of the same platform and the same size on our own roster, on four things: engagement, views, how steady the views are and how much of their content is in the product space. Size is not part of the score (the follower count is shown beside it). A bought audience caps the score. Each score shows how sure it is (high, medium or low) and is marked "limited data" when little is on file. Labels run from "Strong fit" to "Not recommended".
- Selection page: the client's price per creator and the total range, tags and segments, the brief and the scores; "Score this selection" answers the brief questions (goal, platforms, countries, gender, age groups, product space) for a selection that has none; "Request a quote" sends it to the account manager.
- Campaign report: shown for live campaigns. Lists every post with views, reach and engagement, progress against the goals, and an overall verdict (e.g. on track or behind target). Numbers refresh once every 24 hours. Figures marked as estimates are replaced by the creators' real insights once approved. There is also a one-screen dashboard view and a CSV download.

ACCOUNT AND CREDITS
- Clients sign in to HELVY Connect with their work email and a one-time 6-digit code (it expires in 10 minutes). Personal addresses (Gmail, Outlook.com and similar) can't sign in. The HelloVoice team signs in on the admin; admin access is given person by person (info@hellovoice.co.uk). Older shared links still ask for their own access code.
- AI credits: tapping options in this chat is free; a typed question uses 1 credit, a scored shortlist with reasons 5, "Add more like these" 3, "Creators like this" 2 and "Find a replacement" 2. ALL AI is free while the client has an active campaign (from its start date until 30 days after its end date). Credits are earned by completing the profile (up to 30), inviting a colleague (+20) and finishing the 3-minute tour (+5); more can be requested from the profile.
- The 3-minute tour plays the real portal on sample data (Northwind Pharma · Ramadan Skincare) in four chapters: Brief Helvy, Build your shortlist, Check & book, Track results. Replay it from Help or the profile.
- ROI Calculator: inside a selection, on its own page in the profile, or in this chat. Campaign types: Awareness (views, reach), Engagement (interactions, engagement rate), Traffic (tracking-link clicks); several can be picked at once. Results are ranges, rounded, with a line saying for how many of the creators we hold measured data; the market does not change them. The client's total budget feeds a planner that suggests a mix of creator sizes per platform and, for an open selection, up to three ways to improve it (add or remove creators, a second post, another platform), ranked by performance and never by price. After a campaign the estimate's ranges are compared with the live results. No sales or revenue figures: HelloVoice tracks up to the tracking link.
- Selections: the owner approves or rejects each creator (with an optional reason); "Add more like these" adds creators like the approved ones as Under review; "Creators like this" on a card shows three look-alikes; a rejected creator gets "Find a replacement".

WHAT THE ASSISTANT CANNOT DO
- It cannot book creators, promise availability or dates, negotiate prices or discounts, or share anything about other clients. For these, offer to pass the request to the account manager.
""".strip()
